nk><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/directed-at-delhi-govt-officials-court-dismisses-plea-seeking-fir-against-rekha-gupta-over-hanuman-remark/articleshow/135609967.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/directed-at-delhi-govt-officials-court-dismisses-plea-seeking-fir-against-rekha-gupta-over-hanuman-remark/articleshow/135609967.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T20:08:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135611871,imgsize-87434.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Living near a highway toll plaza? New FASTag rule offers annual pass of up to Rs 3,000, but there's a catch]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/living-near-a-highway-toll-plaza-new-fastag-rule-offers-annual-pass-of-up-to-rs-3000-but-theres-a-catch/articleshow/135609104.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135609104.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Residents living within 20 km of National Highway toll plazas can apply for a Concessional Local Pass. The pass costs Rs 1,500 or Rs 3,000 annually, depending on the plaza's location. To qualify, motorists must have a functional FASTag, and their vehicle must be non-commercial. The scheme aims to reduce toll expenses for eligible residents but has specific restrictions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/living-near-a-highway-toll-plaza-new-fastag-rule-offers-annual-pass-of-up-to-rs-3000-but-theres-a-catch/articleshow/135609104.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/living-near-a-highway-toll-plaza-new-fastag-rule-offers-annual-pass-of-up-to-rs-3000-but-theres-a-catch/articleshow/135609104.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-06T19:17:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org